    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&id=8a78839e9fd3ba7b01a01f684da36ea2&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Facilities Technician III - Maintenance and Groundskeeper",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Position: Facilities Technician III - Maintenance and Groundskeeper Location: Yankton, SD Job Id: 325 # of Openings: 1 This is a non-exempt, full-time position and must adhere to the regulations stipulated in the Mount Marty University Employee Handbook. The Mount Marty University Facilities Tech III Groundskeeper position is responsible for the overall maintenance, upkeep, and aesthetic appearance of the grounds and outdoor areas of the Mount Marty University campus. This includes landscaping, turf management, tree and shrub care, hardscape maintenance, and seasonal tasks such as snow removal and leaf cleanup. The Groundskeeper plays a vital role in ensuring a safe, clean, and welcoming environment for employees, visitors, and the public. Mission: We strive to maintain a high quality of service in a timely manner. We do this by providing quality support through effective and experienced management. By supporting MMU, the facilities department is committed to establish and maintain a safe, clean, attractive and effective physical environment for the campus community, as well as to provide high quality support in a cost-effective manner. Key Responsibilities: Turf Management: ​ Mow, trim, and edge lawns and turf areas using a variety of equipment (mowers, trimmers, edgers). Apply fertilizer, pesticides, and herbicides in accordance with safety guidelines and regulations. Oversee irrigation systems, including monitoring, adjusting, and repairing sprinkler heads and lines, and winterizing sprinkler systems. Aerating, seeding, and sodding as needed to maintain healthy and lush turf. Landscaping and Horticulture: ​ Plant, cultivate, and maintain flower beds, shrubs, trees, and other plant life. Prune and trim trees and shrubs to promote healthy growth and maintain a neat appearance. Remove weeds and debris from landscaped areas. Mulch beds and around trees and shrubs. Hardscape and General Maintenance: ​ Maintain and repair walkways, paths, and parking lot surfaces. Clean and maintain outdoor furniture, benches, and other fixtures. Empty trash receptacles and manage recycling in outdoor areas. Pick up litter and debris to ensure the grounds are free of trash. Seasonal Tasks: ​Fall: Rake and blow leaves, and prepare grounds for winter. Winter: Perform snow and ice removal from walkways, entrances, and parking lots using shovels, snow blowers, and snowplows. Apply de-icing agents as needed to ensure safety. Spring: Prepare grounds for the growing season, including cleaning up winter debris, aerating, planting and watering. Equipment Operation and Maintenance: ​ Operate and maintain a variety of groundskeeping and shop equipment, including mowers (riding and push), tractors, trimmers, edgers, blowers, chainsaws, snow blowers, and plows. Perform routine maintenance on equipment and MMU fleet vehicles such as checking fluids, sharpening blades, and cleaning. Report any equipment malfunctions or maintenance needs to the supervisor. Schedule fleet vehicle maintenance, repairs, and inspections. Safety and Compliance: ​ Adhere to all safety protocols and use personal protective equipment (PPE) as required. Store and handle chemicals and fuels safely and in compliance with regulations. Maintain a clean and organized work area. Identify and report any safety hazards on the grounds. Other Duties as assigned: ​ Be available for 24 hour ON-CALL basis, some night and weekend work. Work Overtime as required in campus emergencies, severe weather conditions, and special events. Complete work orders for your area to standard. Maintain proper records for your area, fill out work orders, conduct inventories of parts on hand, order parts needed, complete any specific reports for equipment in your area. Perform preventative maintenance and implement new PM’s to extend life cycle of assets, asset reliability, and reduce operational expenses. Supervise, train, and support student employees assigned to your area. Perform event set ups and office furniture moves. May perform all duties of a Facility Technician 1 and 2. Assist facilities staff or other tasks assigned by Director of Operations or Director of Facilities and Maintenance. Qualifications: High School Diploma or equivalent 1-3 years of experience in groundskeeping, landscaping, or a related field Valid drivers license Knowledge and Skills: ​ Knowledge of plants, turf, and tree care best practices. Ability to safely operate and perform basic maintenance on groundskeeping equipment. Knowledge of safe chemical handling and application. Familiarity with snow and ice removal techniques. Strong attention to detail and a high standard for quality work. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Physical Requirements: ​ Ability to stand, walk, bend, stoop, and lift for extended periods. Ability to lift and carry up to 100 pounds. Willingness to work outdoors in various weather conditions (heat, cold, rain, snow). Ability to perform physically demanding tasks. Other: ​ Commercial fertilizer/herbicide applicator's license must be obtained. Commitment to the Mission of Mount Marty University. About MMU: Located on a beautifully maintained 80-acre campus along the bluffs of the Missouri River, Mount Marty's hallmark is outstanding teaching, small class size, and a strong commitment to the liberal arts in the Catholic, Benedictine tradition. The University has been noted regionally for its strong science programs. The campus is minutes away from Lewis & Clark Lake, one of South Dakota's most popular recreation areas, and is within driving distance of the Twin Cities and Omaha. Application Process: Applicants must submit a letter of application, resume, and the name and e-mail addresses of three references. Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. More detailed information about Mount Marty University, including the mission statement, can be found on our website. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Mount Marty University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&id=8a78839ea13353c501a13bc2755d1580&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Campus Safety Officer - Part-time",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Position: Campus Safety Officer - Part-time Location: Yankton, SD Job Id: 339 # of Openings: 1 Position Overview Mount Marty University invites applications for a Campus Safety Officer (CSO). This is a part-time, non-benefits eligible position that must adhere to the regulations stipulated in the Mount Marty University Employee Handbook. Campus Safety Officers ( C SO) will assist in providing safety to  individuals on campus property and maintaining the security of campus buildings, facilities, parking lots, walkways, and grounds of the University. C SOs provide escort services and other safety services as needed and perform routine security and public safety patrol duties to maintain a safe environment for Mount Marty University and Sacred Heart Monastery. Officers must remain alert to all unusual activity especially emergency situations and provide first-line response, emergency management and/or referral if necessary. Qualifications CSOs must be able to stand and walk for long periods of time and operate security systems; the duties assigned are completed by foot patrol. Must have a valid driver's license. This is a night shift position. Commitment to the mission of Mount Marty University. Applicants are required to pass a standard background check. About MMU Located on a beautifully maintained 80-acre campus along the bluffs of the Missouri River, Mount Marty's hallmark is outstanding teaching, small class size, and a strong commitment to the liberal arts in the Catholic Benedictine tradition.  The campus is minutes away from Lewis & Clark Lake, one of South Dakota's most popular recreation areas, and is within driving distance of the Twin Cities and Omaha. Application Instructions Applicants for this position must submit a letter of application, resume, and the name and e-mail addresses of three references.  These materials will be submitted online to Careers at Mount Marty . Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Mount Marty University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&id=8a78839f9de0710c019e1d2a2e4601ea&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Staff Accountant",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Position: Staff Accountant Location: Yankton, SD Job Id: 307 # of Openings: 1 This is a non-exempt full-time position and must adhere to the Mount Marty University handbook(s). The Staff Accountant provides essential support for the University's accounting functions. The Staff Accountant will work closely with the VP for Finance regarding university accounting, including journal entries, reconciliations, and audit preparation. Duties and Responsibilities System Administration ​ Assist in the administration of Anthology Finance by learning to configure financial codes, supporting the maintenance of the chart of accounts, and assisting with user security Financial Reporting ​ Prepare materials for annual Financial Statement and Financial Aid Single Audit Gather information for annual reporting and tax filings, including 990, IPEDs, and other federally required reports Prepare and process accurate and timely invoices for federal, state, and private grants by compiling all necessary supporting documentation to ensure expenditures align with grantor guidelines and University policy Serve as a primary point of contact for the campus community regarding budget-to-actual inquiries Financial Reconciliation ​ Collaborate with Accounts Payable, Accounts Receivable, and Payroll to ensure accurate and timely monthly close and reconciliation processes Maintain Fixed Asset & Depreciation schedules and balance sheet reconciliations Coordinate with the Financial Aid office on all Business Office transactions, including drawing federal funds and reconciling aid disbursements Other Duties ​ File sales and quarterly payroll reports timely Participate in special projects as assigned Perform additional duties as assigned by the Vice President for Finance and Administration Required Skills and Competencies Proficiency in Microsoft Excel and Word; Anthology Finance preferred Demonstrated customer service, multitasking, and confidentiality management skills Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in accounting Relevant accounting experience Commitment to the mission and values of Mount Marty University About MMU Located on a beautifully maintained 80-acre campus along the bluffs of the Missouri River, Mount Marty's hallmark is outstanding teaching, small class size, and a strong commitment to the liberal arts in the Catholic, Benedictine tradition. The University has been noted regionally for its strong science programs. The campus is minutes away from Lewis & Clark Lake, one of South Dakota's most popular recreation areas, and is within driving distance of the Twin Cities and Omaha. Application Instructions Applicants must submit a letter of application, resume, and the name and e-mail addresses of three references. Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. More detailed information about Mount Marty University, including the mission statement, can be found on our website. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Mount Marty University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&id=8a7883a8a13c124d01a144d6a2300605&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Associate Registrar",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Position: Associate Registrar Location: Yankton, SD Job Id: 342 # of Openings: 1 Overview: Mount Marty University seeks an ambitious professional for the role of full-time Associate Registrar. The Associate Registrar will serve in a vital leadership and operational role in the Office of the Registrar, ensuring the integrity, accuracy, and security of academic records. A key feature of this position is commitment to comprehensive cross-training across all functional areas of the department. The ideal candidate is an adaptable, proactive team player eager to master diverse administrative systems and step into any role within the office to support student success and operational continuity. This position is scheduled to begin in January 2027, though a later start date may be considered for the ideal candidate. Roles and Responsibilities: Oversees the day-to-day interpretation, implementation, and communication of academic policies and procedures of the university Assures efficient and accurate delivery of Registrar’s office functions Collaborates with the Admission Office to evaluate and record transfer coursework Coordinates with academic leaders to create class schedules and assign classroom space Maintain and update the University catalog Serves as School Certifying Official for U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs education benefits Chairs Commencement Committee Assists with degree audit configuration and student degree completion reviews Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required; prior experience in higher education registration, admissions, or records management preferred High accuracy and attention to detail in data entry Strong critical thinking, problem-solving, and analytical capabilities Ability to manage multiple priority projects concurrently with minimal supervision Excellent interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills Commitment to the mission of Mount Marty University About the University: Located on a beautifully maintained 80-acre campus along the bluffs of the Missouri River, Mount Marty's hallmark is outstanding teaching, small class size, and a strong commitment to the liberal arts in the Catholic Benedictine tradition. The campus is minutes away from Lewis and Clark Lake, one of South Dakota's most popular recreation areas, and is within driving distance of the Twin Cities, Kansas City, and Omaha. Application Process: Applicants must submit a letter of application, resume, and the name and e-mail addresses of three references. More detailed information about Mount Marty University, including the mission statement, can be found on our website . Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Mount Marty University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&id=8a7883ac995981c201995e1d723c3214&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Bus Driver - Part-Time",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Position: Bus Driver - Part-Time Location: Yankton, SD Job Id: 216 # of Openings: 1 Bus Driver Mount Marty University is looking for part-time bus drivers to provide transportation for members of our athletic teams and students. All candidates must have or be able to receive a Class C Commercial Drivers License, from the State of South Dakota or State of their residence. Some overnight travel may be required. The ideal candidate must be committed in principle and practice to Mount Marty University’s mission as a Catholic and Benedictine university rooted in the Liberal Arts. About MMU Located on a beautifully maintained 80-acre campus along the bluffs of the Missouri River, Mount Marty's hallmark is outstanding teaching, small class size, and a strong commitment to the liberal arts in the Catholic Benedictine tradition.  The campus is minutes away from Lewis & Clark Lake, one of South Dakota's most popular recreation areas, and is within driving distance of the Twin Cities and Omaha. Application Instructions Applicants for this position must submit a letter of application, resume, and the name and e-mail addresses of three references.  These materials will be submitted online to Careers at Mount Marty. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Mount Marty University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&id=8a78859f9fd3baa0019ff150c0d4680c&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Learning Technology Support Specialist",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Position: Learning Technology Support Specialist Location: Yankton, SD Job Id: 323 # of Openings: 1 This is a full-time position and must adhere to the regulations stipulated in the Mount Marty University Employee Handbook. The Learning Technology Support Specialist provides support for technology used by faculty and students to further the mission of Mount Marty University. Mission: To assist the Information Technology Department in supporting the Universities learning technology needs. Duties and Responsibilities: Provide learning management system support for faculty and students. Assist faculty with the creation of static and video content for traditional, hybrid and distance learning classes. Research advances in educational technology and make recommendations for implementation at Mount Marty University. Serve as the primary point of contact for faculty for computer hardware and software. Facilitate the improvement, repair, and maintenance of lab and classroom technology. Create and provide training programs for students, faculty and staff on new and existing technology. Maintain an accurate inventory of learning technology used across campus. Maintain and improve training documents provided by ITSS and vendors. Work with ITSS team to provide an IT infrastructure that can support existing and new technology initiatives. Provide technology support and training to visitors using campus resources. Support and improve distance learning capabilities. Responsible for set-up and support of audio/visuals needs including live streams during on-campus events. Additional duties as assigned by VP of Technology. Qualifications: Associate or Bachelor Degree or equivalent combination of education and experience. Familiarity with learning management systems. Ability to communicate effectively across a variety of platforms. Comfortable speaking in front of large groups. Demonstrated technical and customer services skills. Commitment to the mission of Mount Marty University. About MMU: Located on a beautifully maintained 80-acre campus along the bluffs of the Missouri River, Mount Marty's hallmark is outstanding teaching, small class size, and a strong commitment to the liberal arts in the Catholic, Benedictine tradition. The University has been noted regionally for its strong science programs. The campus is minutes away from Lewis & Clark Lake, one of South Dakota's most popular recreation areas, and is within driving distance of the Twin Cities and Omaha. Application Process: Applicants must submit a letter of application, resume, and the name and e-mail addresses of three references. Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. More detailed information about Mount Marty University, including the mission statement, can be found on our website. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Mount Marty University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&id=8a78879e9e46f5fc019e4bc789ad3265&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Track & Field Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Position: Track & Field Graduate Assistant Location: Yankton, SD Job Id: 315 # of Openings: 1 Academic Requirements This position is a Graduate Assistantship. Candidates must hold a bachelor's degree and meet eligibility requirements for admission into the Mount Marty University's Master of Education in Coaching Leadership Program upon hire. In order to be considered for the Master’s Program, you must have a 2.75 GPA, three letters of reference from a supervisor, coach, professor, or colleague, and a 1-2 page essay explaining your purpose, goals, and commitment to this coaching program. Interested applicants can apply here. Compensation Candidate will receive a 2/3 tuition waiver from Mount Marty’s Master of Education in Coaching Leadership Program and $2,500 academic stipend. Additional income opportunities will be available during the off-season. Mount Marty Athletics Athletics is responsible for operations of all athletics teams, meeting the requirements of National Association of Intercollegiate Athletics (NAIA) and Great Plains Athletic Conference (GPAC) regulations. Mount Marty University Athletic Department, in accordance with the mission of the university, seeks to provide all students a variety of experiences which will promote and exemplify excellence in sportsmanship and athletic performance, enhance their education, prepare them for service to the human community, and provide a unique view of the university. The Athletic Department strives to provide the following services to the student-athlete: Enhance their education and educational opportunities. Develop character building. Positive and enjoyable experience. Appreciate giving back to the community through service. The Athletic Department strives to provide the following services to the university: Assist in the recruitment of new students. Assist in the fund raising efforts of the university. Assist in the visibility and public relations efforts of the university Essential Duties Assist with the development and implementation of training plans for designated event group(s) during indoor and outdoor track & field seasons.  Ideally, we are looking for someone who has high jump, long jump, and triple jump experience and/or experience with discus, shot put, javelin, weight throw, and hammer throw Coach student-athletes as assigned during practices and meets. Provide oversight and evaluation of student-athletes’ daily progress Recruit prospective student athletes in compliance with University-developed goals and within NAIA guidelines. Recruitment may include making initial contact with prospective students and families, assisting with campus visits, and maintaining regular contact with recruits May participate in event scheduling, budget management, procurement of equipment, all aspects of meet management for collegiate and high school events, and fundraising The employee will be assigned by the immediate supervisor to perform other duties as needed or to perform other reasonably-related duties Application Instructions Applicants must submit materials online at Careers at Mount Marty. Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. More detailed information about Mount Marty University, including the mission statement, can be found on our website. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Mount Marty University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&id=8a7887a19de07068019dfdf83c2b5493&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Position: Athletic Trainer Location: Yankton, SD Job Id: 302 # of Openings: 1 This is a full time, exempt position that must adhere to the regulations stipulated in the Mount Marty University Handbook. In collaboration with the team physician, the Athletic Trainer provides preventative care, emergency care, clinical diagnosis, therapeutic intervention, and rehabilitation of injuries and medical conditions for Mount Marty’s intercollegiate athletic programs. This role serves as a vital communication link between the athlete, physician, coach, and family to determine the best route of treatment and return-to-play timeline. Mission To provide athletes with, and educate both athletes and coaches about, the care and prevention of athletic injuries. Duties and Responsibilities Clinical Care & Rehabilitation Coordinate the prevention, care, evaluation, and rehabilitation of injuries for varsity and junior varsity athletes Perform primary and secondary surveys or evaluations of all athletic-related injuries Responsible for taping, bracing, and padding of athletic-related injuries Deliver appropriate therapeutic modalities and distribute protocols for therapeutic exercise and rehabilitation Monitor ABC’s, CPR, First Aid, and other critical interventions during injury assessments Manage necessary referrals of musculoskeletal and other injuries to the appropriate medical provider and coordinate student-athlete appointments Work under the direction of the Team Physician to provide “medical clearance” for all injured student-athletes Administrative and Operations Direct and supervise the daily operation of the athletic training room and coordinate work-study students Maintain and protect health, insurance, injury, and other necessary records (via Sportsware) ensuring strict confidentiality and compliance Assist in developing the training room budget and initiating the purchase of supplies and equipment Implement and coordinate emergency action plans for all athletic venues Maintain administrative records including injury reports, treatments, and insurance documentation Communication and Support Provide medical coverage before, during, and after games/events; responsible for game/event preparation (ice, water, med kits, biohazard receptacles) Consult, advise, and cooperate with coaches and athletes regarding wellness decisions and injury status Assist in the organization and coordination of community education programs in sports medicine, fitness, and wellness Maintain state licensure and national certification by completing necessary CEUs and required CPR/AED/First Aid certifications Perform other duties as assigned by the Athletic Director and Head Athletic Trainer Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree in Athletic Training required; Master’s degree in Athletic Training or related field from a CAATE accredited program preferred Experience: Two (2) years of post-graduate experience in the athletic training field (or equivalent) preferred Certifications & Licensure: ​BOC Certified Athletic Trainer in good standing Current South Dakota State licensure (or eligible to obtain) Current CPR/AED/First Aid for the Professional Rescuer or Basic Life Support for Healthcare Providers Commitment: Demonstrated commitment to the mission of Mount Marty University Physical Requirements and Working Conditions Schedule Adaptability: Must demonstrate extreme flexibility; the schedule is subject to frequent, last-minute changes due to weather, travel, and post-season play. The position requires nights, weekends, and holidays. Physical Demands: Ability to stand, walk, and sit for extended periods. Must be able to lift and carry up to 50 pounds (coolers, kits, equipment) and occasionally up to 100 pounds. Environmental Exposure: Frequent exposure to outdoor weather conditions and responsibility for monitoring environmental safety for athletes. Travel: Ability to travel with athletic teams for away competitions as assigned. About MMU Located on a beautifully maintained 80-acre campus along the bluffs of the Missouri River, Mount Marty's hallmark is outstanding teaching, small class size, and a strong commitment to the liberal arts in the Catholic, Benedictine tradition. The University has been noted regionally for its strong science programs. The campus is minutes away from Lewis & Clark Lake, one of South Dakota's most popular recreation areas, and is within driving distance of the Twin Cities and Omaha. Application Instructions Applicants must submit a letter of application, resume, and the name and e-mail addresses of three references. Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. More detailed information about Mount Marty University, including the mission statement, can be found on our website. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Mount Marty University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&id=8a7887a8a03fc2be01a0585919b81a40&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Facility Technician I",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Position: Facility Technician I Location: Yankton, SD Job Id: 327 # of Openings: 1 This is a non-exempt, full-time position and must adhere to the regulations stipulated in the Mount Marty University Handbooks. The Facility Technician I cleans and maintains facilities/grounds to enhance the appearance of the buildings. Mission : The facilities department is committed to establishing and maintaining a safe, clean, attractive and effective physical environment for the campus community, as well as to provide high quality service and support in a cost-effective and timely manner. Duties and Responsibilities: Performs a variety of cleaning to ensure sanitary conditions are met to a level that floors and base molding shine and/or are bright and clean; colors are fresh, no buildup in corners or along walls, all vertical and horizontal surfaces have a freshly cleaned or polished appearance and have no accumulation of dust, dirt, marks, streaks, smudges, or fingerprints, lights all work and fixtures are clean, washroom and shower fixtures and tile gleam and are odor free, supplies are adequate, trash containers are clean and odor free Scrubs, mops, waxes and polishes floors using dry and wet mops, wax applicators, buffers, and floor machines Perform basic routine and preventive maintenance on facilities such as re-lamping fixtures, snow removal, ceiling tile replacement, painting, clearing drains, and general repairs Moves and arranges furniture Conduct work in a safe, productive, and environmentally friendly manner Be familiar and comply with the safety regulations and use safety equipment which apply to tools and chemicals you work wit h 7:00-3:30, and some night and weekend work Work overtime as required in campus emergencies, severe weather conditions and special events Supervise, train and support student employees assigned to you Maintain a friendly atmosphere within the department and the campus community Perform other duties as assigned by Associate Vice President of Facilities and Auxiliary Services and Director of Facilities Operations Perform the following tasks at the beginning of the work shift, before/after all breaks, at the end of the work shift, and frequently throughout the work shift; check/respond to email and submit/update scheduled (CMMS) tasks Ability to learn, and use computerized technology to communicate, monitor campus systems, and record keeping per department procedures Perform basic maintenance and operation of equipment; including saws, drills, routers and other miscellaneous tools to complete assigned maintenance tasks Perform basic installation/application of finishes, including caulking, painting, staining, and coatings Work to maintain shop cleanliness and that it is up to standards Communicate effectively and professionally with the public, staff, and students Support graduation ceremonies and other special events Snow removal as needed Qualifications: A High school diploma/GED or equivalent experience Ability to lift objects weighing up to 75 lbs and work off of ladders Valid driver’s license Commitment to the mission of Mount Marty University Scope of Work: This is basic work in a wide variety of cleaning, maintenance and repair of campus buildings, facilities and grounds.  A general knowledge of all disciplines is required.  Performs varied tasks such as primary responsibility for routine, cleaning, maintenance, repair of facilities. Application Process Applicants must submit a letter of application, resume, and the names of three references through the online application system. The review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until filled. About MMU Located on a beautifully maintained 80-acre campus along the bluffs of the Missouri River, Mount Marty's hallmark is outstanding teaching, small class size, and a strong commitment to the liberal arts in the Catholic Benedictine tradition.  The University has been noted regionally for its strong nursing programs. The campus is minutes away from Lewis & Clark Lake, one of South Dakota's most popular recreation areas, and is within driving distance of the Twin Cities and Omaha. More detailed information about Mount Marty University including the mission statement, can be found at http://www.mountmarty.edu Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Mount Marty University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&id=8a7887a8a0abfc8001a0b07b47a71434&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Theology",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Position: Assistant Professor of Theology Location: Yankton, SD Job Id: 331 # of Openings: 1 Overview: Mount Marty University, a Catholic, Benedictine liberal arts institution sponsored by the Sisters of Sacred Heart Monastery, invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Theology position. Appointment is anticipated at the rank of Assistant Professor, though candidates with substantial prior academic experience may be considered for appointment at a higher rank. Review of applications begins immediately. Position is open until filled. Located in Yankton, South Dakota, Mount Marty seeks an outstanding scholar-educator to serve as a primary faculty anchor for theology within the Department of Theology & Philosophy. The successful candidate will demonstrate a primary commitment to undergraduate teaching excellence, a capacity to engage non-majors in the Catholic intellectual tradition, and an active program of scholarly research that enriches classroom instruction. Key Responsibilities: Teach introductory and advanced undergraduate courses in Catholic theology (including Introduction to Theology, Christian Ethics/Moral Theology, and Historical Theology) for both majors and general education students. Collaborate with Philosophy faculty and the Benedictine Leadership Institute (BLI) to teach integrated core curriculum courses examining the relationship between faith, reason, and human flourishing. Engage in interdisciplinary collaboration across academic departments to support mission integration across the curriculum. Maintain an active research agenda producing peer-reviewed scholarly contributions compatible with an undergraduate teaching institution. Provide academic advising, participate in departmental service, and contribute actively to the liturgical, intellectual, and communal life of the university. Qualifications: Education: Ph.D., Th.D., or S.T.D. in Theology or a closely related field in hand by time of appointment. Specialization in Moral Theology or Systematic Theology preferred. Teaching Excellence: Demonstrated success or clear potential in undergraduate instruction, with a proven ability to make complex theological concepts accessible and compelling to a diverse student body. Mission Alignment: Practiced commitment to the Catholic intellectual tradition and a willingness to seek and maintain the mandatum from the Bishop of the Diocese of Sioux Falls pursuant to Ex Corde Ecclesiae . Benedictine Charism: Capacity to integrate Benedictine practices (hospitality, attentive listening, communal searching for truth, and the balance of work and prayer) into teaching and academic citizenship. Work Authorization: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without current or future employer sponsorship. Mount Marty University is not able to sponsor, petition for, provide supporting documentation for, or assume sponsorship of any employment-based visa or work authorization status at this time. Employment is contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check, verification of identity and unrestricted employment authorization as required by federal law, and the ability to be physically present on the Yankton campus by the position start date. Required Application Materials: Cover letter detailing teaching philosophy, research agenda, and specific interest in joining a Catholic, Benedictine liberal arts faculty. Curriculum Vitae. Mission Statement (1–2 pages) outlining your understanding of and commitment to teaching within the Catholic intellectual and Benedictine traditions. One sample syllabus for an introductory undergraduate theology course. One representative scholarly writing sample (article or dissertation chapter, max 30 pages). Contact information for three professional references (at least one addressing teaching capability). About the University Located on a beautifully maintained 80-acre campus along the bluffs of the Missouri River, Mount Marty’s hallmark is outstanding teaching, small class size, and a strong commitment to the liberal arts in the Catholic Benedictine tradition. The campus is minutes away from Lewis and Clark Lake, one of South Dakota’s most popular recreation areas, and is within driving distance of the Twin Cities, Kansas City, and Omaha. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For more information about Mount Marty University and its mission, please visit www.mountmarty.edu. Mount Marty University is an affirmative action, equal opportunity employer. We encourage candidates of all backgrounds to apply. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Mount Marty University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&id=8a7887a8a0abfc8001a0b08574a61881&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Business, Marketing",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Position: Assistant Professor of Business, Marketing Location: Yankton, SD Job Id: 338 # of Openings: 1 Overview: Mount Marty University, a Catholic, Benedictine liberal arts institution sponsored by the Sisters of Sacred Heart Monastery, invites applications for an open rank, tenure-track faculty position in Business with expertise in Marketing. Located in Yankton, South Dakota, Mount Marty seeks a teacher-scholar or an accomplished practitioner who will serve as a primary faculty member for marketing within the Business program. Rank and salary will be commensurate with credentials and experience. The successful candidate will demonstrate a primary commitment to undergraduate teaching, the ability to connect marketing theory to contemporary practice for a broad range of students, and sustained professional or scholarly activity that enriches classroom instruction. Mount Marty welcomes applications from candidates early in their academic careers and from those moving into teaching from professional practice. New faculty are supported by the university’s Teaching and Learning Center, which provides mentoring, instructional design assistance, and ongoing development for colleagues new to the classroom. Review of applications begins immediately. Position is open until filled. Key Responsibilities: Teach the breadth of the marketing curriculum at the undergraduate level, including areas such as principles of marketing, consumer behavior, digital and social media marketing, and marketing research, along with foundational business courses required across the program, at a load of twelve credit hours per semester. Contribute to course offerings in adjacent areas such as Economics, Operations Management, Information Systems, and Human Resource Management as institutional need requires. Coordinate course scheduling with the Registrar’s Office and participate in ongoing program assessment. Provide academic advising to Business majors and support student professional development, internships, and career preparation. Work collaboratively with colleagues in the Business Department and across the university to support mission integration in the curriculum. Contribute actively to the intellectual and communal life of the university through departmental and institutional service. Qualifications: Education: An earned doctorate in Business Administration, Marketing, or a closely related field is preferred by time of appointment. Candidates who are ABD will be considered provided all doctoral requirements are completed in the fall of 2027. Candidates holding a master’s degree in Business Administration or a related field together with substantial professional experience in marketing will also be given full consideration. Commitment to Teaching: Demonstrated effectiveness or clear promise as an undergraduate teacher, with the ability, or evident capacity to develop the ability, to make marketing concepts accessible and compelling to a diverse student body and to connect classroom learning to current practice. Professional and Scholarly Activity: Evidence of continuing scholarly work, professional practice, or applied engagement in the discipline appropriate to an undergraduate teaching institution. Mission Alignment: Commitment in principle and practice to Mount Marty University’s mission as a Catholic and Benedictine university rooted in the liberal arts. Benedictine Charism: Capacity to integrate Benedictine practices of hospitality, attentive listening, communal searching for truth, and the balance of work and prayer into teaching and academic citizenship. Work Authorization: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without current or future employer sponsorship. Mount Marty University is not able to sponsor, petition for, provide supporting documentation for, or assume sponsorship of any employment-based visa or work authorization status at this time. Employment is contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check, verification of identity and unrestricted employment authorization as required by federal law, and the ability to be physically present on the Yankton campus by the position start date. Required Application Materials: Applicants must submit the following through the university’s online application system: A letter of application addressing the position’s requirements and responsibilities. A current curriculum vitae. A statement of teaching philosophy. A statement describing how your experience and commitments align with Mount Marty’s Catholic and Benedictine mission. Contact information for three professional references, at least one of whom can address teaching capability. About the University Located on a beautifully maintained 80-acre campus along the bluffs of the Missouri River, Mount Marty’s hallmark is outstanding teaching, small class size, and a strong commitment to the liberal arts in the Catholic Benedictine tradition. The campus is minutes away from Lewis and Clark Lake, one of South Dakota’s most popular recreation areas, and is within driving distance of the Twin Cities, Kansas City, and Omaha. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For more information about Mount Marty University and its mission, please visit www.mountmarty.edu. Mount Marty University is an affirmative action, equal opportunity employer. We encourage candidates of all backgrounds to apply. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Mount Marty University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&id=8a7887a8a0abfc8001a0b09c088322f1&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Business, Finance",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Position: Assistant Professor of Business, Finance Location: Yankton, SD Job Id: 337 # of Openings: 1 Overview: Mount Marty University, a Catholic, Benedictine liberal arts institution sponsored by the Sisters of Sacred Heart Monastery, invites applications for an open rank, tenure-track faculty position in Business with expertise in Finance. Located in Yankton, South Dakota, Mount Marty seeks a teacher-scholar or an accomplished practitioner who will serve as a primary faculty member for finance within the Business program. Rank and salary will be commensurate with credentials and experience. The successful candidate will demonstrate a primary commitment to undergraduate teaching, the ability to connect financial theory to practice for a broad range of students, and sustained professional or scholarly activity that enriches classroom instruction. Mount Marty welcomes applications from candidates early in their academic careers and from those moving into teaching from professional practice. New faculty are supported by MMU’s Teaching and Learning Center, which provides mentoring, instructional design assistance, and ongoing development for colleagues new to the classroom. Review of applications begins immediately. Position is open until filled. Key Responsibilities: Teach the breadth of the finance curriculum at the undergraduate level, along with foundational business courses required across the program, at a load of twelve credit hours per semester. Contribute to course offerings in adjacent areas such as Economics, Operations Management, Information Systems, and Human Resource Management as institutional need requires. Coordinate course scheduling with the Registrar’s Office and participate in ongoing program assessment. Provide academic advising to Business majors and support student professional development, internships, and career preparation. Work collaboratively with colleagues in the Business Department and across the university to support mission integration in the curriculum. Contribute actively to the intellectual and communal life of the university through departmental and institutional service. Qualifications: Education: An earned doctorate in Business Administration, Finance, or a closely related field is preferred by time of appointment. Candidates who are ABD will be considered provided all doctoral requirements are completed in the fall of 2027. Candidates holding a master’s degree in Business Administration or a related field together with substantial professional experience in finance will also be given full consideration. Commitment to Teaching: Demonstrated effectiveness or clear promise as an undergraduate teacher, with the ability, or evident capacity to develop the ability, to make complex financial concepts accessible and compelling to a diverse student body. Professional and Scholarly Activity: Evidence of continuing scholarly work, professional practice, or applied engagement in the discipline appropriate to an undergraduate teaching institution. Mission Alignment: Commitment in principle and practice to Mount Marty University’s mission as a Catholic and Benedictine university rooted in the liberal arts. Benedictine Charism: Capacity to integrate Benedictine practices of hospitality, attentive listening, communal searching for truth, and the balance of work and prayer into teaching and academic citizenship. Work Authorization: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without current or future employer sponsorship. Mount Marty University is not able to sponsor, petition for, provide supporting documentation for, or assume sponsorship of any employment-based visa or work authorization status at this time. Employment is contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check, verification of identity and unrestricted employment authorization as required by federal law, and the ability to be physically present on the Yankton campus by the position start date. Required Application Materials: Applicants must submit the following through the university’s online application system: A letter of application addressing the position’s requirements and responsibilities. A current curriculum vitae. A statement of teaching philosophy. A statement describing how your experience and commitments align with Mount Marty’s Catholic and Benedictine mission. Contact information for three professional references, at least one of whom can address teaching capability. About the University: Located on a beautifully maintained 80-acre campus along the bluffs of the Missouri River, Mount Marty’s hallmark is outstanding teaching, small class size, and a strong commitment to the liberal arts in the Catholic Benedictine tradition. The campus is minutes away from Lewis and Clark Lake, one of South Dakota’s most popular recreation areas, and is within driving distance of the Twin Cities, Kansas City, and Omaha. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For more information about Mount Marty University and its mission, please visit www.mountmarty.edu. Mount Marty University is an affirmative action, equal opportunity employer. We encourage candidates of all backgrounds to apply. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Mount Marty University"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883c68ab5129a018abce5b6dc034a&id=8a7887a8a0abfc8001a0b0d8b1203bef&source=&lang=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biology",
      "description": "Mount Marty University Home Position: Assistant Professor of Biology Location: Yankton, SD Job Id: 336 # of Openings: 1 Overview: Mount Marty University, a Catholic, Benedictine liberal arts institution sponsored by the Sisters of Sacred Heart Monastery, invites applications for a full-time, in-person, tenure-track position in Biology. Located in Yankton, South Dakota, Mount Marty seeks a broadly trained biologist who will serve as the primary faculty member for teaching human anatomy and physiology. Appointment is anticipated at the rank of Assistant Professor, though candidates with substantial prior academic experience may be considered for appointment at a higher rank. The successful candidate will demonstrate a primary commitment to undergraduate teaching, the ability to teach across the biology curriculum, and sustained professional or scholarly activity that enriches classroom instruction. MMU’s biology professors serve biology majors, students preparing for pre-professional careers and students in the university’s nursing program. The department also contributes substantially to the General Education program, so the successful candidate will teach students at a wide range of preparation levels and career intentions. Mount Marty welcomes applications from candidates early in their academic careers. New faculty are supported by the university’s Teaching and Learning Center, which provides mentoring, instructional design assistance, and ongoing development for colleagues new to the classroom. Review of applications begins immediately. Position is open until filled. Key Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate courses in human anatomy and physiology, including the accompanying laboratory sections with an Anatomage table, as the primary teaching assignment for this position. Teach additional courses across the biology curriculum as departmental need requires, with microbiology and genetics as the most likely assignments. Contribute to the General Education program. Provide academic advising. Work collaboratively with colleagues in Biology and across the university to support mission integration in the curriculum. Contribute actively to the intellectual and communal life of the university through departmental and institutional service. Qualifications: Education: An earned doctorate in Biology or a closely related field is preferred by the time of appointment. Candidates who are ABD will be considered provided all doctoral requirements are completed prior to the fall of 2027. Graduate preparation, research, or teaching emphasis in human anatomy and physiology is preferred. Commitment to Teaching: Prior experience as instructor of record for full-semester undergraduate biology courses with an accompanying laboratory is preferred, though not necessary. Candidates should demonstrate the ability to make rigorous biological content accessible and compelling to majors, pre-professional students, nursing students, and general education students alike. Professional and Scholarly Activity: Evidence of continuing scholarly work, professional practice, or applied engagement in the discipline appropriate to an undergraduate teaching institution, including the capacity to involve undergraduates in that work. Mission Alignment: Commitment in principle and practice to Mount Marty University’s mission as a Catholic and Benedictine university rooted in the liberal arts. Benedictine Charism: Capacity to integrate Benedictine practices of hospitality, attentive listening, communal searching for truth, and the balance of work and prayer into teaching and academic citizenship. Work Authorization: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without current or future employer sponsorship. Mount Marty University is not able to sponsor, petition for, provide supporting documentation for, or assume sponsorship of any employment-based visa or work authorization status at this time. Employment is contingent upon satisfactory completion of a background check, verification of identity and unrestricted employment authorization as required by federal law, and the ability to be physically present on the Yankton campus by the position start date. Required Application Materials: Applicants must submit the following through the university’s online application system: A letter of application addressing the position’s requirements and responsibilities. A current curriculum vitae. A statement of teaching philosophy. A teaching record listing each course for which you have served as instructor of record, indicating the term, the institution, approximate enrollment, and whether a laboratory section was attached. Courses in which you assisted, proctored, or taught laboratory sections under another instructor should be listed separately. A statement describing how your experience and commitments align with Mount Marty’s Catholic and Benedictine mission. Contact information for three professional references, at least one of whom can address teaching capability. About the University: Located on a beautifully maintained 80-acre campus along the bluffs of the Missouri River, Mount Marty’s hallmark is outstanding teaching, small class size, and a strong commitment to the liberal arts in the Catholic Benedictine tradition. The campus is minutes away from Lewis and Clark Lake, one of South Dakota’s most popular recreation areas, and is within driving distance of the Twin Cities, Kansas City, and Omaha. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For more information about Mount Marty University and its mission, please visit www.mountmarty.edu. Mount Marty University is an affirmative action, equal opportunity employer. We encourage candidates of all backgrounds to apply. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by Mount Marty University"
    }
